From: OpenWrt RV220W research <rv220w-research@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: b53: include firmware-described CPU ports in setup

The B53 chip table describes the ports normally enabled by a given switch
variant.  On BCM53115 it lists external ports 0-4 and IMP port 8, but the
silicon also supports port 5 as a Broadcom-tag-capable CPU port.  Boards such
as the Cisco RV220W wire both port 5 and port 8 to separate Ethernet MACs and
describe both links as DSA CPU ports.

b53_configure_vlan() iterates dev->enabled_ports when it creates the default
PVID/VLAN domain.  A firmware-described CPU port absent from the static chip
mask is therefore skipped: its default VLAN tag is left at the bootloader
value and it is not added to the default VLAN entry.  Port-based VLAN affinity
can still look correct while untagged ingress frames are rejected by the
ordinary 802.1Q membership check before reaching that CPU conduit.

Merge the DSA CPU-port mask into dev->enabled_ports before switch reset and
configuration.  The DSA topology has already been parsed at this point, and
b53_possible_cpu_port() continues to constrain which ports can be used as
Broadcom-tag-capable conduits.  This lets the existing generic VLAN setup
initialize every active CPU conduit consistently without adding board policy
or a hard-coded WAN VID.

---
 drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c
@@ -925,6 +925,17 @@ static int b53_setup(struct dsa_switch *ds)
 	unsigned int port;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Static chip data describes the usual enabled ports, but firmware may
+	 * expose an additional valid CPU conduit.  Include every DSA CPU port
+	 * before the default PVID/VLAN setup iterates enabled_ports, otherwise
+	 * the secondary conduit can retain a stale PVID and remain outside the
+	 * default VLAN entry even though its port-based VLAN mask is correct.
+	 *
+	 * num_ports already spans the highest hardware port for B53 devices.
+	 */
+	dev->enabled_ports |= (u16)dsa_cpu_ports(ds);
+
 	/* Request bridge PVID untagged when DSA_TAG_PROTO_NONE is set
 	 * which forces the CPU port to be tagged in all VLANs.
 	 */
-- 
2.49.0
